Hi Phil and other,

I am concerned with the fit statistics generated by the m2 command in mirt for a 7-factor graded response model, as they are very inconsistent with the very good to excellent fit statistics for each of the 7 domains modeled individually, and with the fit statistics for the corresponding CFA model estimated in Lavaan. In particular, I am concerned that estimated covariances between factors may not be properly incorporated into the computation of residual matrix used for M2 fit statistics.

Here is my mirt model, estimated on a sample of about 1100 observations. The items are all ordinal with 6 response categories:
"   resDom = res8, res11, res13, res15
    proDom = pro2, pro3, pro4, pro5, pro7
    intDom = int1, int2, int3, int4, int5, int7, int8, int10
    actDom = act2, act5, act6, act8, act12
    socDom = soc3, soc6, soc7, soc8, soc9
    heaDom = hea1, hea3, hea4, hea6, hea7
    disDom = dis3, dis4, dis5, dis6
    COV=resDom*proDom*intDom*actDom*socDom*heaDom*disDom"

Estimation:
mirt(data, model, itemtype='graded', method='MHRM')

The discrimination parameters and associated standardized loadings look good:
